        "thinking": "There are many errors. The key ones:\n1. `Cannot find module '../../../server/src/...' or its corresponding type declarations` - these are from the `exclude` I added which is now excluding server/src from the program. Since the server package is imported via relative paths (not package imports), TypeScript tries to find the type info but can't because I excluded server/src.\n\n2. `r2-run-log-store.ts` - comparing `\"local_file\"` to `\"r2\"` - this means the `RunLogHandle` type from server has `store: \"local_file\"` as the only discriminant, not `\"r2\"`.\n\n\n3. `hyperdrive.ts` - Cannot find module 'postgres' - the CF package uses postgres indirectly via db/hyperdrive.ts. I'm realizing that TypeScript's `exclude` doesn't actually prevent files from being included when they're imported from an included file—it only prevents them from matching the `include` glob patterns, so the exclude list isn't the real culprit here.\n\nLooking at the actual error messages, these imports weren't failing before I added the exclude, which suggests the issue might be with how `moduleResolution: \"bundler\"` handles `.js` extension imports that point to `.ts` files—unlike `NodeNext`, it doesn't automatically resolve `./foo.js` to `./foo.ts`.\n\nThe exclude list is likely the culprit here since TypeScript can't load files from excluded directories when resolving imports. I should remove it and instead address the root causes directly: adding missing dependencies like `postgres` to the Cloudflare package, and fixing the import paths to use proper extensions or relative paths that TypeScript can resolve. I'm realizing the `exclude` list in tsconfig actually does prevent TypeScript from resolving modules outside the package, even when using `moduleResolution: bundler` — so excluding `../../server/src` is blocking those imports from being found at all.\n\nThe simplest fix is to remove the `exclude` list entirely and accept the pre-existing errors from the db package, since those are just noise from type-checking under CF's bundler settings anyway.",
